post_install() {
    cat <<'MSG'
==> LSW: before the first VM start
    - /dev/udmabuf: the GPU device needs it. The module loads at boot
      (/usr/lib/modules-load.d/lsw.conf); to use it now:
          sudo modprobe udmabuf
          sudo udevadm trigger --sysname-match=udmabuf
      Your login session gets access to it (udev "uaccess"); log out and
      back in if `ls -l /dev/udmabuf` shows no ACL for your user.
    - /dev/kvm must be usable by your user (it is, on a stock Arch).
    - VMs run under your user's libvirt session (qemu:///session): no
      libvirt group membership and no system libvirtd are needed.
    - Shared folders need virtiofsd; OpenCL in the guest needs an OpenCL
      driver on the host (optional dependencies).
    Start "LSW Manager" from the application menu, or run lsw-manager.
MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
    # Nothing to migrate. A running VM keeps the QEMU it was started
    # with until it is shut down and started again.
    :
}
